# `Where` in title case is the wrong case (DS0104), not SQL; only capitals count as SQL.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | Where amount > 1 | Select amount
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..48
  PIPELINE@0..47
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..31
      IDENT@15..20 "Where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..31
        NAME_REF@21..27
          IDENT@21..27 "amount"
        WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
        GT@28..29 ">"
        WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
        LITERAL@30..31
          LONG@30..31 "1"
    WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
    PIPE@32..33 "|"
    WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
    PROJECT_OP@34..47
      IDENT@34..40 "Select"
      WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@41..47
        NAME_REF@41..47
          IDENT@41..47 "amount"
  WHITESPACE@47..48 "\n"

error[DS0104]: unknown operator `Where`
  --> query:1:16
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | Where amount > 1 | Select amount
  |                ^^^^^ operator names are case-sensitive
  |
  = help: write `where`

error[DS0104]: unknown operator `Select`
  --> query:1:35
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | Where amount > 1 | Select amount
  |                                   ^^^^^^ not a DataScript operator
  |
  = help: to choose or compute columns, use `project`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where amount > 1 | project amount
which parses without errors
